//! The practice company (P08 step 8, Q-219, Q-226): Ozark Ridge
//! Landscaping LLC, one synthetic year generated by `cargo xtask
//! gen-sample` into `fixtures/sample/ozark_ridge/`. The figures the design
//! mockups show (`docs/design/README.md`) are computed here from the
//! fixture with exact [`Money`] and pinned by the golden test.
//!
//! "Try the practice company" loads the fixture into a new tenant: the
//! general-service chart, every client and vendor, and each transaction
//! as a journal entry (the invoice, bill and payment forms arrive in
//! P17-P21 and will replace this with real documents, Q-P08h).
//!
//! The fixture also carries the Write Check mockup story (P13 WP0): the
//! vendor Ozark Feed & Seed with its address, default account 5110 and an
//! open bill, the accounts Materials:Plants (5100) and Materials:Mulch &
//! stone (5110), the tags Install and Crew A, the job Hollister Family
//! Trust:Fall bed install, and 1010 checks numbered up to 4417 so the next
//! check is 4418. The loader creates the vendor details and line memos;
//! sub-account parents, tags and jobs are demo-only until the engine
//! import takes them (jobs need U-35).
//!
//! And the P14 money story: two customer payments posted Dr Payments
//! Clearing (10150) / Cr A/R so the engine lists them as waiting to be
//! deposited (`GET /payments/pending-deposits` takes any posted debit to
//! Payments Clearing), the 11/04 bank-file deposit of both, the "Plant sale
//! counter" daily-sales layout and the lender's 11/04 statement. The engine's
//! journal entries carry no contact, so the loader names the customer in
//! the memo, as for every other fixture transaction.

